D = LS – LR The actual level in the receiving room depends on the following:
a) Sound insulation of the separating wall or floor;
b) Area of the separating wall or floor;
c) Volume of the receiving room;
d) Amount of flanking transmission (that is the importance of transmission paths other than the separating wall or floor); and PART D BUILDING SERVICES — SECTION 4 ACOUSTICS, SOUND INSULATION AND NOISE CONTROL
