f) Maintaining proper cable routes — Cable shall not be routed over pipes, conduits, other cabling, ceiling tiles, etc, but shall rest directly on the supporting surface so as to minimize the potential for sharp bends, kinks, etc. Every cable used shall be supported in such a way that it is not exposed to undue mechanical strain so that there is no appreciable mechanical strain on the terminations; and g) Labelling — The cable shall be clearly labelled at both ends, as outlined in the documentation and/or drawing.

