4.3.2 Opening for Feeding of Refuse Chute
Opening, with top or bottom hinged shutters with appropriate lockable latch, shall be provided for convenient accessing of the refuse chute by users. It facilitates total building garbage collection at one single point and provides separate collection for dry and wet garbage. The opening of the refuse chute may have separate receptacles for both wet and dry waste. Mixed waste disposal may not be allowed. For wet waste, there should be a provision for collection of leachate. Chute system shall have the following features:
a) Sanitation system for internal cleaning of chutes, with sprinklers at every floor intake level, with disinfectant cleaning, which may preferably be automatic in operation;
b) Exhaust system with 25 to 35 air changes per hour;
c) Discharge end fire resistant door;
d) Chute may be of masonry, R.C.C pipe, asbestos cement pipe or suitable non- corrosive material, preferably stainless steel. It should be rigid with smooth internal finish, high ductility and alkali/acid resistant properties {see also good practice [E-3(3)]};
e) For fire rating, reference should be made to relevant clauses of Part F ‘Fire and Life Safety’ of this NBCS;
f) Fire sprinklers shall be provided inside chute;
g) Vent shall be installed at roof level to remove foul smell and gases generated;
h) Chute should discharge to trolley directly;
j) Necessary automation of the system may be planned to avoid malfunction by manual operation; and k) All care shall be taken for ensuring accessibility to the chute for persons with disabilities. The opening of the chute shall not be higher than 700 mm and there shall be a clear space of minimum 1 500 mm × 1 500 mm in front of the chute opening to gain easy access even for persons using wheelchairs. There may be high colour contrast provided around the chute opening to make it easy to identify it. The flooring in front of the chute opening may be texturally highly different from the rest of the floor.

