23.5.2 Fabrication Waste Management
Strategies for fabrication waste management include:
a) ordering directly from mills to minimize offcuts;
b) using stock lengths as ordered efficiently to minimize waste. Where possible, splice locations in steel members should be coordinated to fall within standard stock length sizes;
c) recycling and reusing steel fabrication waste, for example, off-cuts, swarf, etc;
d) considering use off-cuts of material, particularly from plate, elsewhere, for example, temporary works, connection fittings, shims, packs, rather than simply scrapping for recycling. Always prioritized reuse over recycling;
e) considering use of machines that facilitate common line cutting of fittings;
f) minimizing coating waste and coating packaging waste, by using intermediate bulk; and g) Minimizing/ avoiding overspray of coatings should ensure operators are properly trained and the appropriate and properly maintained equipment is used.
