8.2.3 General Design Principles
The design of precast slabs is based on the following principles:
a) The precast slab together with any in-situ concrete (for partial depth slab) should be designed as continuous in both the longitudinal and the transverse direction;
b) The joints between slabs should be designed to transmit membrane forces as well as bending moment and shear forces;
c) The effective width of precast slab in the composite beam action shall be calculated as per 8.3.3;
d) The design principles of composite beams involving either full depth or partial depth precast slabs are similar to standard composite decks using cast in-situ reinforced concrete;
e) Vertical shear check of the composite beam shall be done as per 8.3.6; and f) For serviceability limit states, guidelines given in 7.2.2 and 9 shall be followed.

