23.5.3 Sustainable Welding
Strategies for sustainable welding include:
a) Avoiding low productivity processes and using automatic and semi-automatic processes with continuous wire feed, thus using material efficiently and avoiding energy waste;
b) Adopting energy-saving processes such as, inverter-based power sources instead of older regulator/rectifier-based sources, electrically powered pre-heating with temperature control instead of gas flame;
c) Minimizing pre-heat in the welding procedure specification and welding continuously to avoid the need to re-heat; and d) Periodically reviewing welding techniques and weld procedures to make the best use of the latest advancements in welding equipment and consumables, including the selection of joint set-ups and consumables that allow for deeper penetration fillet welds to be achieved, thus potentially reducing the number of weld runs required.

