4.1.3 Glare
Excessive contrast or abrupt and large changes in brightness produce the effect of glare.  When glare is present, the efficiency of vision is reduced and small details or subtle changes in scene cannot be perceived.  It may be, a) direct glare due to light sources within the field of vision;
b) reflected glare due to reflections from light sources or surfaces of excessive brightness; and c) veiling glare where the peripheral field is comparatively very bright.

