The resources should be carefully planned based on the types of project elements and their quantities. The engineer is also responsible for reserving these resources throughout the project duration.  Key feasibility considerations include:
a) Building geometry — Ensure shapes and geometry are as symmetrical and regular as possible;
b) Grid-lines — Column and wall locations should, preferably, follow a standardized pattern;
c) Height clearances — Consideration of clear height expectations between beams and slabs;
d) Grid spacing — Optimize grid spacing to take full advantage of precast elements; and e) Standardization — Standardize elements within one floor and across multiple floors when feasible.

