9.3.1 Haulage Planning
Transportation constraints influence the size and shape of precast elements.  The following factors should be considered in haulage planning:
a) Trailer lengths (standard lengths of 6 m, 12 m, with special cases up to 30 m);
b) Trailer width (typically between 2.4 m to 2.7 m);
c) Height clearance (3.6 m to 4 m, adjustable with low-bed trailers);
d) Weight capacity (25 MT to 35 MT);
e) Special permits for oversized loads that may be needed;
f) Route surveys and permissions to be obtained if crossing bridges or navigating urban areas; and g) Large element transportation time slots through day/night as per local regulations.

