2.1.30 Outdoor Artificial Lighting — Lighting systems specifically designed for exterior environments, intended
to enhance visibility, safety and security during nighttime hours while minimizing adverse environmental and ecological impacts. Key considerations include:
PART D  BUILDING SERVICES — SECTION 1 LIGHTING AND NATURAL VENTILATION
a) Fully shielded — Luminaire designs that emit light only in the downward direction, preventing upward light emissions.  This helps control glare and limits contributions to light pollution;
b) Full cut-off — A luminaire classification where zero light is emitted at or above the horizontal plane of the fixture.  This design minimizes sky glow and enhances lighting efficiency by directing light only where it is needed;
c) Light trespass — The unintended or intrusive illumination of areas beyond the target zone, such as neighbouring properties, streets, or natural habitats.  Light trespass can lead to discomfort, sleep disruption and privacy issues; and d) Sky glow — The diffuse illumination of the night sky caused by artificial lighting, particularly from urban areas.  Sky glow reduces the visibility of stars, interferes with astronomical observations and disrupts nocturnal ecosystems.

